00:43:53,290 --> 00:43:55,626
I know just the guy to talk to.

509
00:43:57,211 --> 00:43:58,879
Get him. Come on.

510
00:44:04,927 --> 00:44:08,055
Hey, yo. Kraze, how you doing, my man?

511
00:44:10,349 --> 00:44:14,478
Hey, you got a new dog. Right on, man.

512
00:44:14,853 --> 00:44:16,689
What's his name?

513
00:44:17,773 --> 00:44:21,735
Yeah, I had a dog like that once,
except maybe like twice as big.

514
00:44:21,944 --> 00:44:23,529
Super-purebred.

515
00:44:23,737 --> 00:44:27,283
Now, me personally, I would train him
to go straight for the nutsack.

516
00:44:27,491 --> 00:44:29,535
Just shut your mouth and show me your money.

517
00:44:29,743 --> 00:44:31,245
I ain't buying, <i>ese</i>.

518
00:44:32,246 --> 00:44:33,914
I'm selling.

519
00:44:43,007 --> 00:44:46,552
Tell me that ain't the finest scante you ever laid eyes on.

520
00:44:47,553 --> 00:44:49,889
Go ahead. Try it.

521
00:44:50,097 --> 00:44:52,683
Hey, poochie. How you doing?

522
00:44:53,475 --> 00:44:55,519
Jesus Christ.

523
00:44:56,270 --> 00:44:59,023
Yeah. Booya! See, what'd I say?

524
00:44:59,899 --> 00:45:01,609
- It's all right.
- It's all right?

525
00:45:01,817 --> 00:45:03,569
It's all right? Yeah, it's all right.

526
00:45:03,777 --> 00:45:07,031
- So what? You're back in business?
- Hell, yeah, I'm back.

527
00:45:07,364 --> 00:45:10,743
With a vengeance. <i>Vato loco</i> gotta make a living.

528
00:45:10,951 --> 00:45:13,704
You know, with your cousin gone away and all...

529
00:45:14,455 --> 00:45:17,166
And listen, homes, about that...

530
00:45:18,792 --> 00:45:21,253
Really broke me up about Emilio.

531
00:45:22,004 --> 00:45:23,964
That dude is like my brother.

532
00:45:24,298 --> 00:45:27,176
- You okay? You talk to him?
- Yeah, I talk to him.

533
00:45:27,509 --> 00:45:31,472
Said when the feds came, you were
out sticking it in some neighbour lady.

534
00:45:31,680 --> 00:45:35,935
- Hey, you know, I got lucky twice.
- I don't know, man.

535
00:45:36,310 --> 00:45:37,853
Emilio...

536
00:45:39,980 --> 00:45:42,358
he thinks maybe you dimed on him.

537
00:45:42,942 --> 00:45:45,986
Whoa, whoa, hey, hey. That is bullshit.

538
00:45:46,820 --> 00:45:48,906
That is bullshit, Krazy, eh?

539
00:45:49,114 --> 00:45:51,742
I should kick his punk ass for even thinking that.

540
00:45:52,326 --> 00:45:54,787
You know what? Next time you talk to Emilio...

541
00:45:54,995 --> 00:45:56,664
you tell him for me, all right?

542
00:46:00,834 --> 00:46:03,879
Why don't you tell him yourself? Made bail this morning.

543
00:46:04,088 --> 00:46:06,966
Go ahead, <i>pendejo</i>. Kick my ass.

544
00:46:07,216 --> 00:46:08,717
Hey, listen...

545
00:46:11,887 --> 00:46:13,806
Where did you get this?

546
00:46:15,724 --> 00:46:18,519
Because I know your little punk ass didn't cook it.

547
00:46:47,631 --> 00:46:51,802
Damn, man. What are you, some kind of nudist?

548
00:46:53,804 --> 00:46:57,099
Yeah, that's some stone-fine tick-tick
you been cooking there, <i>ese</i>.

549
00:46:57,308 --> 00:46:58,934
How about you come work for me?

550
00:47:00,728 --> 00:47:03,355
I'd be willing to sell it to you...

551
00:47:03,898 --> 00:47:05,274
if the price is right.

552
00:47:16,327 --> 00:47:18,370
Out here all by yourself, huh?

553
00:47:26,003 --> 00:47:30,049
Hey, I know you. He was there when I got busted.

554
00:47:30,257 --> 00:47:32,259
- He's with the DEA.
- No.

555
00:47:33,010 --> 00:47:35,512
You <i>rata</i> snitch motherfucker.

556
00:47:35,930 --> 00:47:37,223
Run, Mr. White! Run!

557
00:47:47,650 --> 00:47:49,151
I say we cap them both.

558
00:47:56,617 --> 00:47:58,619
You really cook up that batch?

559
00:48:00,746 --> 00:48:03,249
- Yeah.
- You an artist.

560
00:48:05,125 --> 00:48:07,836
- It's a damn shame.
- Wait.

561
00:48:08,045 --> 00:48:09,421
Wait a minute.

562
00:48:10,130 --> 00:48:14,760
Listen to me. I'll teach you my recipe, huh?

563
00:48:14,969 --> 00:48:17,137
What do you say? You wanna cook like me?

564
00:48:20,516 --> 00:48:22,476
You let us both live...

565
00:48:23,727 --> 00:48:27,356
and I will teach you, huh?

566
00:48:56,844 --> 00:48:58,804
Put the cigarette out.

567
00:49:01,640 --> 00:49:03,017
Please...

568
00:49:46,518 --> 00:49:49,939
Move it, homes. You got all day?

569
00:49:52,691 --> 00:49:54,026
Okay.

570
00:52:19,046 --> 00:52:20,506
Shit!

571
00:54:05,402 --> 00:54:06,987
What happened?

572
00:54:09,698 --> 00:54:12,243
Hey, what'd you do to them?

573
00:54:14,203 --> 00:54:17,915
Red phosphorus in the presence
of moisture and accelerated by heat...

574
00:54:18,123 --> 00:54:20,459
yields phosphorus hydride.

575
00:54:21,543 --> 00:54:23,504
Phosphine gas.

576
00:54:23,921 --> 00:54:26,048
One good whiff and...

577
00:54:50,698 --> 00:54:52,324
We gotta...

578
00:54:54,368 --> 00:54:57,621
We gotta clean this up.

579
00:55:44,919 --> 00:55:46,670
Where were you?

580
00:55:55,054 --> 00:55:56,639
Walt...

581
00:55:59,266 --> 00:56:01,727
I don't know what's been going on with you lately...

582
00:56:01,936 --> 00:56:04,688
- but...
- Nothing, honey. I'm fine.

583
00:56:04,897 --> 00:56:09,109
Whatever it is, I'll tell you this.

584
00:56:09,693 --> 00:56:12,905
I do not like it when you don't talk to me.

585
00:56:14,323 --> 00:56:17,284
The worst thing you can do is shut me out.

586
00:57:03,372 --> 00:57:05,082
Walt...

587
00:57:07,543 --> 00:57:12,006
Oh, Walt, is that you?

